# rule.require.useThen-useWhen-for-shared-results

## .what
capture an operation's result once with test-fns `useThen` / `useWhen`, share it across blocks — no `let`, no repeat calls
- `useThen('it succeeds', async () => op())` — creates a then block; result shared with peer then blocks
- `useWhen('[t1] action', () => { …; return result; })` — wraps a when block; result shared with peer when blocks (idempotency, before/after)
both return a proxy that defers access

## .pattern
```ts
when('[t0] operation is executed', () => {
  const result = useThen('it succeeds', async () => expensiveOperation({ input }));
  then('returns output', () => { expect(result.output).toBeDefined(); });
  then('returns cost', () => { expect(result.cost.total).toBeDefined(); });
});

const responseFirst = useWhen('[t1] registration is called', () =>
  useThen('registration succeeds', async () => registerUser({ email })));
when('[t2] registration is repeated', () => {
  const responseSecond = useThen('still succeeds', async () => registerUser({ email }));
  then('is idempotent', () => { expect(responseSecond.id).toEqual(responseFirst.id); });
});
```

## .enforcement
- same expensive call repeated in adjacent then blocks = blocker
- `let` declared to share an async result across blocks = blocker
